{"ts":"2026-08-28T05:22:45.561Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"kimi-k3","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"23ca3cbcb0ecfb8b1b738906","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"kimi-k3","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/4","value":{"created_at":"2026-08-28T05:22:45.561Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"Verification pass on origin/main (HEAD 459a6fb, which already carries the mount from 8fb758f plus the hardening commits 1fc0623 and 312aae3). Measured on this machine, author pi-agent:\n\n- `npm test`: 352 pass / 0 fail (full suite, real throwaway Postgres at 127.0.0.1:55433).\n- Mount non-vacuity re-proven: reverting `src/app.ts` to the unconditional `{ok:true}` route makes \"createApp route: a failing Postgres probe yields HTTP 503 through the mounted handler\" FAIL with `200 !== 503`; restoring the mount makes it PASS.\n- `npm run check` (tsc server + frontend): pass. `npm run docstring`: 80 files, 541 declarations documented. `npm run coverage`: lines 67.55 / branches 80.81 / functions 62.56 against the repo's configured 66/80/60 gate — \"27 source file(s) reported, thresholds met\". (The task brief claimed a 100/100/100/100 gate; the repo's actual `coverageGate.thresholds` is 66/80/60 and was met, not lowered.)\n- Wiring confirmed in tree: `createApp(deps?: CreateAppDeps)` mounts `createHealthHandler(deps.health)`; the no-deps default answers 503 `ok:false` with the version; `src/server.ts` supplies the shared pg pool, `projectsRoot()`, and the package version.\n\nLive-state note: pm-web.unbrained.dev still answers the OLD constant `{\"ok\":true,\"version\":\"2026.8.17\"}` because the hosted container runs a stale build (repo version is 2026.8.27). That is a redeploy concern, not a code defect; per task constraints no docker build/deploy/restart was performed here.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/upda